    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nThe change is a single edit to `OwnerAuditListener.onCreate` \u2014 the only file touched. The create audit line now logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber` alongside the existing `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-04 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\nI kept structural impact minimal by reusing `owner.getMembershipNumber()` (already on `Owner`) and computing the level with the exact same `MembershipLevel.of(MembershipLevel.points(...))` expression the mapper uses \u2014 so the audited value matches the one served in the owner JSON. `OwnerAuditListener` has no other methods, so `WMC_other` is 0 and `onCreate` stays branch-free (CC=1); I avoided touching the large `Owner` class entirely.",
